  "observations": [
    "Special+0xca and+0xc8 are sign-extended amplitude and seed/rate inputs at5f0f00. The coefficient helper itself accepts signed32-bit inputs. Original float RNG advances only a local copy of seed with1664525*x+1013904223, then takes23 mantissa bits; no shared RNG state changes.",
    "Global97390c is a uint frame counter. Native signed integer load plus2^32 correction preserves that integer in extended precision before rate multiplication; the decompiler float temporary is misleading. Global80b6d8/80b6dc scale amplitude/rate, both PE-image1.0 but runtime inputs remain explicit.",
    "The first coefficient uses sine at phase,2.1phase,4.2phase with stored half/quarter terms. The second uses cosine at negative2.3phase,negative4.4phase,negative1.1phase with stored half/quarter terms. Each frequency product storesfloat32 before angle conversion; exact original operation order and table signs are retained.",
    "CRT global29a9c48 changes large-angle conversion: x87 path truncates to signed64 then low32 wraps, while SSE path returns80000000 on signed32 overflow. Both are explicitly modelled and tested at large uint frame counters. The two32-bit operands of the final scale product fit48 significant bits, so its double product is exact.",
    "5ec590 first copies16DWORDs forward, then writes only second-row4 components as(firstRow*x + secondRow) + thirdRow*z. Whole and forward/backward partial aliases remain defined by this operation order; unused matrix words are copied unchanged.",
    "All245 authored nonzero sway specials across the complete1477-carrier index are included in both conversion modes.2048 signed/magnitude/time coefficient cases plus bounded alias/zero matrices supplement authored data. No computational callback is used.",
    "Shared Animation.PlaybackWide supplies64-significand arithmetic; signed-zero signs are retained separately at exact cancellation/zero stores. Portable source and replay compile only."
  ],
